["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/IsoAutomationLevel/assistiveAutomation", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Level 1 - Assistive automation. The system assists an operator.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/UnitOfMeasure", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property", "_:Nad4cd51dce5b4541a93880c56acdef69", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ismn", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Music Number (ISMN)](https://ismn-international.org/ismn/the-ismn/) is a unique numeric identifier for printed music (notated music) standardized by [ISO 10957](https://www.iso.org/standard/83122.html). It consists of either 10 characters (starting with the letter \"M\" for assignments prior to January 1, 2008) or 13 digits. A 13-digit ISMN is composed of four parts: the GS1 prefix `979-0`, a registrant element, an item element, and a check digit. While elements may be divided by spaces or hyphens for human readability, these separators shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., `9790006538424`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N91f0a4ecc96a4355b83ec2da905739f0", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/country", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/CreationInfo", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property", "_:Nd1ce9aab9b7a492ab98072266db71e4f", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/originatedBy", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/Agent", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/republishedBy", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/iscc", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Content Code (ISCC)](https://iscc.io/) is a content-derived identifier standardized by [ISO 24138](https://www.iso.org/standard/77899.html) for identifying digital assets. ISCC can be used in conjunction with other schemes, such as DOI, ISAN, ISBN, ISRC, ISSN and ISWC. A standard ISCC-CODE is build from multiple ISCC-UNITs. Each unit serve a different purpose. An ISCC-CODE typically look like `ISCC:KACT4EBWK27737D2AYCJRAL5Z36G76RFRMO4554RU26HZ4ORJGIVHDI`.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Dataset/DatasetAvailabilityType/directDownload", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Dataset is publicly available and can be downloaded directly.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
